  "details": "I would like to know what opening the steam menu does to lower CPU. I have included screenshots. As you can see in frametiming, CPU usage just halves. And my FPS meter reports more FPS, despite the room I was in filling up when I was fumbling to make a screenshot of the VR menu, as the steam VR shortcut to make screenshots doesn't work in the menu.\n\nI didn't notice a drop in resolution when opening the steam VR menu. My VR resolution is just set to 100%, and GPU usage doesn't show the same drop.\n\nDoes anyone know what is causing this? I would like this performance during normal play.\n\nI don't use OSC, my avatar doesn't have custom animations. I tried a difference avatar and I got the same result.\n\nI'm using a quest 1 with a wired oculus link. Processor: Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10700F CPU @ 2.90GHz, GPU: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2060 SUPER.",
